          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/retrieval-patterns.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Retrieval Patterns\\ndescription: Techniques for combining and ranking results from multiple retrieval methods.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Retrieval\\n  - concept/Ranking\\n  - pattern/RAG\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Two independent sources; core pattern well-established in production systems.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\n## Hybrid Retrieval\\n\\nHybrid retrieval combines sparse lexical search (e.g. BM25) with dense vector search, then merges the two ranked result sets to capture both exact term matches and semantic similarity.\\n\\n**Components:**\\n- **Sparse lexical search:** Exact term matching using algorithms like BM25, effective for rare identifiers (error codes, product SKUs) and precise terminology\\n- **Dense vector search:** Semantic matching using embeddings, captures intent and conceptual similarity\\n- **Merging:** Results from both methods are ranked and combined, often via [[reciprocal-rank-fusion]]\\n\\n**Performance characteristics:**\\nHybrid retrieval consistently outperforms either method alone on queries that mix rare identifiers with natural language intent. It has become the default retrieval pattern in production RAG systems.\\n\\n## Reciprocal Rank Fusion\\n\\nUse reciprocal rank fusion for robust retrieval.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Production RAG systems source (2026)\\n\u0022}"
